.TH RICHMACK 1 "August 2026" "RichmackOS v0.6.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
richmack \- terminal-first personal computing assistant
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B richmack
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGUMENTS ]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B RichmackOS
is a lightweight Linux personal computing assistant.

It performs deterministic filesystem, project, search, memory, duplicate,
documentation, and retrieval tasks locally while delegating expensive AI
inference and embeddings to an Ollama server running at:

.EX
http://richmack.local:11434
.EE

The Debian server does not need to run a local LLM.

.SH COMMANDS

.SS System

.TP
.B richmack status
Show system status including hostname, uptime, RAM, disk, indexed files,
projects, memories, AI server state, model count, and RAG availability.

.TP
.B richmack doctor
Check required commands and connectivity to richmack.local.

.SS Indexing and Search

.TP
.B richmack scan PATH
Scan a directory and update the local SQLite file and project index.

Example:

.EX
richmack scan ~
.EE

.TP
.B richmack search QUERY
Search indexed filenames and paths.

Example:

.EX
richmack search kubernetes
.EE

.TP
.B richmack large
Show the largest indexed files.

.TP
.B richmack duplicates
Find exact duplicate files using size comparison followed by SHA-256.

No files are automatically deleted.

.SS Git Projects

.TP
.B richmack repos
List indexed Git repositories with stack, branch, dirty state, remote,
and last commit date.

.SS Memory

.TP
.B richmack remember TEXT
Store a local memory.

Example:

.EX
richmack remember "The Debian server stores the RAG database."
.EE

.TP
.B richmack memories
List stored memories.

.TP
.B richmack recall QUERY
Search stored memories.

.TP
.B richmack forget ID
Delete a stored memory by ID.

.SS Skills

.TP
.B richmack skill add NAME COMMAND
Create a reusable shell skill.

Example:

.EX
richmack skill add diskfree "df -h"
.EE

.TP
.B richmack skill list
List stored skills.

.TP
.B richmack skill show NAME
Display the command associated with a skill.

.TP
.B richmack skill run NAME
Run a skill after interactive confirmation.

.SS Plugins

.TP
.B richmack plugins
List files in the RichmackOS plugin directory.

Plugins are stored in:

.EX
~/.richmackos/plugins
.EE

.SS AI

.TP
.B richmack ai QUESTION
Ask a one-shot question through RichmackAI.

Example:

.EX
richmack ai "Explain systemd."
.EE

.TP
.B richmack chat
Start interactive RichmackAI chat.

The underlying command is:

.EX
richmackai --chat
.EE

RichmackAI supports model selection and saving output.

Examples:

.EX
richmackai -m gemma2:2b --chat
richmackai -o ~/answer.txt "Explain chmod 755."
richmackai --chat -o ~/chat.txt
.EE

.SS RAG

.TP
.B richmack rag QUESTION
Ask a question against the indexed Richmack RAG knowledge base.

Example:

.EX
richmack rag "What CPU does this computer have?"
.EE

The underlying command is:

.EX
richmackrag ask QUESTION
.EE

Richmack RAG stores source documents, text chunks, vectors, and SQLite
metadata on the Debian server.

Embedding and generation are handled remotely by richmack.local.

.TP
.B richmackrag index PATH
Index a file or directory.

.TP
.B richmackrag search QUESTION
Show the most relevant retrieved chunks.

.TP
.B richmackrag stats
Show RAG database statistics.

RAG answers include references and an Evidence Match score.

Evidence Match measures retrieval relevance and is not a guarantee of
factual accuracy.

.SS Documentation

.TP
.B richmack readme PATH
Generate a project README using the remote LLM.

Example:

.EX
richmack readme .
.EE

Generated files are stored under:

.EX
~/Readme/PROJECT_NAME/README.md
.EE

.SH ARCHITECTURE

.EX
Debian Server
|
+-- Filesystem index
+-- SQLite
+-- Project catalog
+-- Memory
+-- Skills
+-- Plugins
+-- RAG retrieval
|
+------ LAN ------> richmack.local:11434
                    |
                    +-- Ollama
                    +-- Granite
                    +-- Nomic embeddings
.EE

