.SH FILESYSTEM WATCHER

.TP
.B richmack watch start
Start and enable the incremental RichmackOS filesystem watcher.

.TP
.B richmack watch stop
Stop the watcher.

.TP
.B richmack watch restart
Restart the watcher.

.TP
.B richmack watch status
Display systemd status for the watcher.

.TP
.B richmack watch log
Display recent watcher events.

.TP
.B richmack watch follow
Follow watcher events live through the systemd journal.

The watcher uses Linux inotify and updates the RichmackOS SQLite file index
incrementally.

The watcher does not move, rename, or delete user files.

High-churn and sensitive directories such as .git, .cache, .ssh, .config,
node_modules, virtual environments, and RichmackOS internal directories are
excluded.

The service name is:

.EX
richmack-watch.service
.EE

.SH AUTOMATIC RAG INDEXING

The RichmackOS filesystem watcher automatically sends supported changed
documents to the Richmack RAG index.

Supported extensions include:

.EX
.txt
.md
.markdown
.rst
.csv
.json
.yaml
.yml
.html
.EE

When a supported file is created or modified, RichmackOS first updates the
filesystem SQLite index and then executes:

.EX
richmackrag index FILE
.EE

Embedding computation is performed remotely through the Ollama service on
richmack.local.

PDF files are not automatically indexed until PDF text extraction support is
enabled.

.SH KNOWLEDGE INBOX

RichmackOS uses the following recommended directory for automatic document
ingestion:

.EX
~/Knowledge-Inbox
.EE

Documents placed in this directory are detected by the incremental
filesystem watcher.

Supported text-based documents are automatically submitted to
.B richmackrag
for indexing.

Supported automatic extensions currently include:

.EX
.txt
.md
.markdown
.rst
.csv
.json
.yaml
.yml
.html
.EE

.SH DOCUMENT INGESTION WORKFLOW

The normal workflow is:

.EX
Remote Computer
      |
      | scp / rsync
      v
~/Knowledge-Inbox
      |
      v
inotify watcher
      |
      +----> RichmackOS filesystem SQLite index
      |
      v
richmackrag index
      |
      v
text chunks
      |
      v
richmack.local embedding API
      |
      v
vectors stored on Debian
      |
      v
richmack rag QUESTION
      |
      v
Granite response with references
.EE

.SH SENDING DOCUMENTS

From another machine, a document can be copied to the Debian server with:

.EX
scp ~/Desktop/aws-notes.txt \
    wisdom@192.168.1.78:~/Knowledge-Inbox/
.EE

Multiple files:

.EX
scp ~/Documents/*.txt \
    wisdom@192.168.1.78:~/Knowledge-Inbox/
.EE

A directory:

.EX
scp -r ~/Documents/DevOps \
    wisdom@192.168.1.78:~/Knowledge-Inbox/
.EE

For repeated synchronization, use rsync:

.EX
rsync -av \
    ~/Documents/DevOps/ \
    wisdom@192.168.1.78:~/Knowledge-Inbox/DevOps/
.EE

.SH VERIFYING AUTOMATIC INDEXING

View watcher activity:

.EX
richmack watch log
.EE

Search the normal file index:

.EX
richmack search aws-notes
.EE

View RAG statistics:

.EX
richmackrag stats
.EE

Inspect semantic retrieval:

.EX
richmackrag search "IAM permissions"
.EE

Ask the indexed document collection:

.EX
richmack rag "What do my documents say about IAM permissions?"
.EE

.SH MANUAL DOCUMENT INDEXING

Files already present on the server may be manually indexed with:

.EX
richmackrag index ~/Documents
.EE

or:

.EX
richmackrag index ~/Knowledge-Inbox
.EE

.SH DAILY WORKFLOW

A typical RichmackOS knowledge workflow is:

.EX
1. Send documents to ~/Knowledge-Inbox
2. Watcher detects new or changed files
3. Filesystem metadata is updated
4. Supported documents are RAG indexed
5. Embeddings are generated on richmack.local
6. Vectors remain stored on Debian
7. Query with richmack rag
8. Review references and Evidence Match
.EE

.SH AI AND RAG COMMANDS

Use ordinary AI without document grounding:

.EX
richmack ai "Explain Linux namespaces."
.EE

Use interactive AI:

.EX
richmack chat
.EE

Use indexed documents:

.EX
richmack rag "What do my documents say about Linux namespaces?"
.EE

.SH PDF INGESTION

PDF files are not yet automatically ingested into the RAG database.

The current RAG implementation directly reads text-based files.

Future PDF support can use
.BR pdftotext (1)
before chunking and embedding.

.SH YOUTUBE KNOWLEDGE INGESTION

.TP
.B richmack youtube channels
List configured YouTube channels.

.TP
.B richmack youtube sync
Download and clean subtitles for recent videos from configured channels.

The default limit is ten videos per channel.

.TP
.B richmack youtube sync --limit N
Set the number of recent videos inspected per channel.

.TP
.B richmack youtube sync --channel CHANNEL
Sync one configured channel.

.TP
.B richmack youtube status
Display YouTube ingestion state.

.TP
.B richmack youtube search QUERY
Search locally stored transcript text.

Clean transcripts are stored under:

.EX
~/Knowledge-Inbox/YouTube
.EE

The filesystem watcher automatically submits new transcript text files to
RichmackRAG. Embeddings are generated remotely by richmack.local.

The ingestion workflow is:

.EX
YouTube
  |
yt-dlp
  |
VTT subtitles
  |
clean text
  |
Knowledge-Inbox
  |
watcher
  |
RichmackRAG
  |
remote embeddings
  |
query with richmack rag
.EE

.SH RAG NAMESPACES

RichmackOS supports scoped RAG retrieval.

Unscoped behavior remains available:

.EX
richmack rag "QUESTION"
.EE

A scope can be selected with:

.EX
richmack rag --scope SCOPE "QUESTION"
.EE

Supported scopes include:

.EX
all
youtube
docs
projects
system
.EE

Examples:

.EX
richmack rag --scope youtube \
    "What do my YouTube transcripts say about robotics?"

richmack rag --scope docs \
    "What do my documents say about IAM?"

richmack rag --scope projects \
    "How is RichmackOS organized?"

richmack rag --scope system \
    "What CPU does this server use?"
.EE

Scoped retrieval reduces unrelated-document contamination.

.SH YOUTUBE QUERY FILTERS

.TP
.B richmack youtube ask CHANNEL --latest QUESTION
Query only the newest transcript for a channel.

.TP
.B richmack youtube ask CHANNEL --days N QUESTION
Query transcripts uploaded during the last N days.

.TP
.B richmack youtube ask CHANNEL --since YYYY-MM-DD QUESTION
Query transcripts uploaded on or after the specified date.

.TP
.B richmack youtube ask CHANNEL --video VIDEO_ID QUESTION
Query one specific YouTube transcript.

Examples:

.EX
richmack youtube ask fireship --latest \
    "What did this video discuss?"

richmack youtube ask danny-jones --days 30 \
    "What topics came up most often?"

richmack youtube ask tim-ferriss --since 2026-08-01 \
    "What themes were discussed?"
.EE

YouTube filters are applied before semantic retrieval so unrelated channel
transcripts are not considered.

.SH RESEARCH OUTPUT EMBEDDING

YouTube Research Mode stores derived research artifacts under:

.EX
~/Knowledge/Research/youtube/CHANNEL/
.EE

Each run produces:

.EX
YYYY-MM-DD_HHMMSS.md
YYYY-MM-DD_HHMMSS.json
latest.md
latest.json
.EE

The RichmackOS filesystem watcher recursively monitors the home directory.

Because Markdown and JSON are supported automatic RAG file types, research
artifacts are automatically submitted to:

.EX
richmackrag index FILE
.EE

This produces two searchable knowledge layers:

.EX
raw YouTube transcript
        |
        v
RAG embedding

derived research brief
        |
        v
RAG embedding
.EE

The raw transcript should be treated as the original source.

Generated Markdown and JSON research files are derived summaries and
extracted knowledge produced by the configured language model.

.SH YOUTUBE RESEARCH WORKFLOW

The full YouTube research pipeline is:

.EX
YouTube channel
      |
      v
yt-dlp
      |
      v
subtitle download
      |
      v
VTT cleanup
      |
      v
plain transcript
      |
      v
~/Knowledge-Inbox/YouTube/
      |
      v
watcher
      |
      v
RichmackRAG embedding
      |
      v
richmack youtube research
      |
      +----> summary pass
      |
      +----> extraction pass
      |
      +----> research pass
      |
      v
Markdown + JSON
      |
      v
~/Knowledge/Research/youtube/
      |
      v
watcher
      |
      v
RichmackRAG embedding
.EE

.SH YOUTUBE RESEARCH COMMANDS

Research the latest three transcripts for one channel:

.EX
richmack youtube research chill-dude-explains --limit 3
.EE

Research all configured channels:

.EX
richmack youtube research --all --limit 3
.EE

Use a specific model:

.EX
richmack youtube research chill-dude-explains \
    --limit 3 \
    --model gemma3:4b
.EE

Research only recent videos:

.EX
richmack youtube research danny-jones \
    --days 30 \
    --limit 10
.EE

.SH YOUTUBE KNOWLEDGE LAYERS

RichmackOS distinguishes between:

.TP
.B Raw transcripts
Original cleaned subtitle text downloaded from YouTube.

.TP
.B Research briefs
Model-generated summaries, keywords, tags, resources, claims,
research queries, people, organizations, and concept relationships.

Both may be embedded into RichmackRAG, but only the raw transcript should
be considered the original source record.

.SH YOUTUBE MULTI-PASS RESEARCH

RichmackOS YouTube Research Mode uses several focused model passes instead
of asking one model response to perform every extraction task.

The pipeline is:

.EX
transcripts
    |
direct URL extraction
    |
summary pass
    |
keyword pass
    |
entity pass
    |
resource pass
    |
research pass
    |
merge
    |
final JSON + Markdown
.EE

Run research on one channel:

.EX
richmack youtube research chill-dude-explains --limit 3
.EE

Run research on every configured channel:

.EX
richmack youtube research --all --limit 3
.EE

The default research model is:

.EX
gemma3:4b
.EE

A model may be overridden with:

.EX
richmack youtube research fireship \
    --limit 3 \
    --model MODEL
.EE

Research run fragments are stored beneath:

.EX
~/Knowledge/Research/youtube/CHANNEL/runs/TIMESTAMP/
.EE

Each run contains:

.EX
summary.json
keywords.json
entities.json
resources.json
research.json
final.json
final.md
.EE

The most recent combined result is also stored as:

.EX
~/Knowledge/Research/youtube/CHANNEL/latest.json
~/Knowledge/Research/youtube/CHANNEL/latest.md
.EE

.SH YOUTUBE RESOURCE EXTRACTION

Extract resources from recent channel transcripts:

.EX
richmack youtube resources chill-dude-explains --limit 3
.EE

Resource extraction includes both deterministic URL discovery and a focused
language-model resource analysis.

Potential resource types include websites, books, studies, tools, apps,
courses, organizations, training programs, named procedures, legal doctrines,
medical techniques, psychological techniques, research institutions, and
frameworks.

Explicit URLs are extracted directly from source text before model analysis.

The language model is instructed never to invent missing URLs.

The latest resource extraction is stored under:

.EX
~/Knowledge/Research/youtube/CHANNEL/resources-latest.json
.EE

.SH YOUTUBE

RichmackOS provides YouTube subtitle ingestion, transcript storage, automatic
RAG indexing, scoped queries, summaries, combined briefings, and interactive
chat.

.SH YOUTUBE CHANNEL MANAGEMENT

List configured channels:

.EX
richmack youtube channels
.EE

Add a channel:

.EX
richmack youtube add-channel \
    CHANNEL_KEY \
    "DISPLAY NAME" \
    "YOUTUBE URL"
.EE

Example:

.EX
richmack youtube add-channel \
    renaissance-periodization \
    "Renaissance Periodization" \
    "https://www.youtube.com/@RenaissancePeriodization/videos"
.EE

Remove a channel:

.EX
richmack youtube remove-channel CHANNEL_KEY
.EE

Channel configuration is stored in:

.EX
~/.richmackos/youtube-channels.json
.EE

.SH YOUTUBE SYNCHRONIZATION

Synchronize recent videos from every configured channel:

.EX
richmack youtube sync --limit 3
.EE

Synchronize one channel:

.EX
richmack youtube sync \
    --channel fireship \
    --limit 3
.EE

RichmackOS uses yt-dlp to retrieve subtitles or automatic subtitles.

Subtitle data is cleaned and saved as plain text beneath:

.EX
~/Knowledge-Inbox/YouTube/
.EE

Previously ingested video IDs are tracked so future runs can skip duplicate
work.

.SH YOUTUBE AUTOMATIC RAG INDEXING

New transcript text files are automatically detected by the RichmackOS
filesystem watcher.

The ingestion path is:

.EX
YouTube
   |
yt-dlp
   |
VTT subtitles
   |
clean text
   |
Knowledge-Inbox
   |
filesystem watcher
   |
RichmackRAG
   |
embedding API on richmack.local
   |
local vector database
.EE

Embedding generation is performed remotely through Ollama on richmack.local.

.SH YOUTUBE SEARCH

Search locally stored transcript text:

.EX
richmack youtube search QUERY
.EE

.SH YOUTUBE ASK

Ask a RAG-grounded question about one configured channel:

.EX
richmack youtube ask fireship \
    "What programming topics are discussed?"
.EE

Restrict retrieval to the newest transcript:

.EX
richmack youtube ask fireship \
    --latest \
    "What did this video discuss?"
.EE

Channel-scoped retrieval prevents unrelated documents from entering the
YouTube answer context.

.SH YOUTUBE SUMMARIES

Summarize recent transcripts for one channel:

.EX
richmack youtube summarize \
    chill-dude-explains \
    --limit 3
.EE

Summarize all configured channels:

.EX
richmack youtube summarize \
    --all \
    --limit 3
.EE

The default summarizer model is:

.EX
gemma3:4b
.EE

The summarizer displays terminal progress while preparing and generating the
report.

.SH YOUTUBE COMBINED SUMMARY

Generate individual channel summaries followed by one cross-channel briefing:

.EX
richmack youtube summarize \
    --all \
    --limit 3 \
    --combined
.EE

The combined briefing can synthesize themes, differences, keywords, tags,
people, organizations, resources, research leads, claims, and practical
takeaways.

.SH YOUTUBE CHAT

Open an interactive YouTube chat for one channel:

.EX
richmack youtube chat chill-dude-explains
.EE

Open an interactive chat across all configured channels:

.EX
richmack youtube chat --all
.EE

The chat maintains conversational history within the session.

Interactive commands include:

.EX
/clear
/quit
.EE

A terminal progress bar is displayed while the model is generating an answer.

The default chat model is:

.EX
gemma3:4b
.EE

YouTube source material is treated as untrusted content rather than executable
instructions.

.SH YOUTUBE WORKFLOW

A typical workflow is:

.EX
1. richmack youtube add-channel KEY "NAME" URL
2. richmack youtube sync --limit 3
3. richmack youtube summarize CHANNEL --limit 3
4. richmack youtube summarize --all --limit 3 --combined
5. richmack youtube ask CHANNEL "QUESTION"
6. richmack youtube chat CHANNEL
.EE

The experimental multi-pass research subsystem is not part of the active
YouTube workflow.

